job	desc	Submit and manage jobs via the bridge server
job	help	
job	examples	
job accept	desc	Accept a job awaiting review (needs_review -> done)
job accept	help	
job accept	examples	
job accept	flag config	path to the gofer config file
job accept	flag no-deliver	accept without delivering the worktree branch (skip the project's delivery)
job accept	flag note	optional note recorded with the acceptance
job accept	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
job accept	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
job answer	desc	Answer a job's pending interaction (an approval takes one of its option ids)
job answer	help	
job answer	examples	
job answer	flag config	path to the gofer config file
job answer	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
job answer	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
job approve	desc	Approve a job awaiting approval (awaiting_approval -> queued, then it runs). A person's decision: refused inside an agent session
job approve	help	
job approve	examples	
job approve	flag config	path to the gofer config file
job approve	flag note	optional note recorded with the approval
job approve	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
job approve	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
job cancel	desc	Cancel a running job
job cancel	help	
job cancel	examples	
job cancel	flag config	path to the gofer config file
job cancel	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
job cancel	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
job comment	desc	Comment on a job. A mention like @omp or @reviewer in a USER's comment dispatches a job for it; inside a job (GOFER_JOB_ID set) the comment is recorded as that agent's and dispatches nothing
job comment	help	
job comment	examples	
job comment	flag config	path to the gofer config file
job comment	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
job comment	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
job comments	desc	List a job's comment thread
job comments	help	
job comments	examples	
job comments	flag config	path to the gofer config file
job comments	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
job comments	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
job delete	desc	Delete terminal job records and keep a deletion audit
job delete	help	
job delete	examples	
job delete	flag config	path to the gofer config file
job delete	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
job delete	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
job delete	flag yes	confirm deletion without an interactive prompt
job deliver	desc	Deliver a done --worktree job now: merge its branch, push it, or push it and open a pull / merge request
job deliver	help	
job deliver	examples	
job deliver	flag branch	remote branch name (default: the project's delivery.branch template)
job deliver	flag config	path to the gofer config file
job deliver	flag draft	open the request as a draft
job deliver	flag dry-run	show the delivery plan without executing it
job deliver	flag mode	merge | push | pr (default: the job's / project's delivery mode)
job deliver	flag ready	open the request ready for review (not a draft)
job deliver	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
job deliver	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
job end	desc	End a resident ACP session job and release its lock
job end	help	
job end	examples	
job end	flag config	path to the gofer config file
job end	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
job end	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
job findings	desc	List the 「发现但不碰」 (out-of-scope findings) items of a job's report; --create-issues files them in the current repo's tracker
job findings	help	
job findings	examples	
job findings	flag config	path to the gofer config file
job findings	flag create-issues	create one issue per finding in the current repository's tracker (description names the job) and print the new ids
job findings	flag priority	priority of the created issues, 0 (highest)..4
job findings	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
job findings	flag tag	comma-separated tags of the created issues
job findings	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
job follow-up	desc	Queue a follow-up request for a running job's session
job follow-up	help	
job follow-up	examples	
job follow-up	flag config	path to the gofer config file
job follow-up	flag drop	drop queued follow-up by its position
job follow-up	flag list	list queued follow-ups
job follow-up	flag review-each	pause for human review after this follow-up
job follow-up	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
job follow-up	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
job interactions	desc	List a job's interactions (questions, choices, approval requests)
job interactions	help	
job interactions	examples	
job interactions	flag config	path to the gofer config file
job interactions	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
job interactions	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
job list	desc	List jobs with optional filters (tag/agent/runner/since/...)
job list	help	
job list	examples	
job list	flag agent	filter by agent key
job list	flag all	include internal delivery jobs (messenger)
job list	flag caller	filter by caller id
job list	flag config	path to the gofer config file
job list	flag limit	max jobs to return (0 = server default)
job list	flag plan	filter by plan id (exact match)
job list	flag project	filter by project key
job list	flag runner	filter by runner key
job list	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
job list	flag session	filter by session id (exact match; lists a session's turns)
job list	flag since	keep jobs with started_at >= since (unix seconds)
job list	flag source-job	filter by source job id (list jobs derived from it)
job list	flag status	filter by status (awaiting_approval/paused_for_update/queued/running/recovering/pending_interaction/needs_review/done/failed/cancelled/timeout/rejected)
job list	flag tag	filter by tag (exact element match)
job list	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
job list	flag wf	filter by workflow id (list that workflow's step-jobs)
job logs	desc	Read a job's stdout/stderr logs
job logs	help	
job logs	examples	
job logs	flag config	path to the gofer config file
job logs	flag head	read first lines
job logs	flag lines	number of lines (last N; first N with --head; default 20 with --head/--tail)
job logs	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
job logs	flag stderr	read stderr stream
job logs	flag stream	log stream: stdout|stderr
job logs	flag tail	read last lines
job logs	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
job redact	desc	Redact literals or patterns from a terminal job
job redact	help	
job redact	examples	
job redact	flag config	path to the gofer config file
job redact	flag literal-from-stdin	read the literal from stdin; it is never accepted as an argument
job redact	flag pattern	RE2 pattern to redact (repeatable)
job redact	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
job redact	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
job reject	desc	Reject a job awaiting review (needs_review -> rejected; --resume continues it with the note) or a job awaiting approval (-> cancelled, never run; the reason is optional)
job reject	help	
job reject	examples	
job reject	flag config	path to the gofer config file
job reject	flag note	why it is refused (required for a delivery, optional for a held job; also the continuation's prompt with --resume)
job reject	flag reason	alias of --note
job reject	flag resume	continue the work: start a new job with the note as its prompt (not for a held job)
job reject	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
job reject	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
job rerun	desc	Re-submit a job from its original request (fresh idempotency key)
job rerun	help	
job rerun	examples	
job rerun	flag config	path to the gofer config file
job rerun	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
job rerun	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
job rerun	flag watch	watch the new job's stream until it finishes
job resume	desc	Resume a job's underlying agent session as a new job (same runner)
job resume	help	
job resume	examples	
job resume	flag agent	continue with another agent of the same session family (e.g. claude-acp <-> claude); default = the source's agent
job resume	flag agent-budget-cost-usd	soft USD cost budget handed to the agent, which winds the run up itself once spent, e.g. 2.5 (only agents with an agent_budget mapping — others are refused)
job resume	flag agent-budget-tokens	soft token budget handed to the agent, which winds the run up itself once spent (accepts 50000 / 50k / 1.5m; only agents with an agent_budget mapping, e.g. suga — others are refused). Keep it below --max-tokens
job resume	flag config	path to the gofer config file
job resume	flag env	extra env var for the resumed process: K=V (repeatable; overrides the env inherited from the source agent/job). The value is stored with the new job (request_json) - never pass secrets here
job resume	flag lock	narrow the directory lock to this project-relative path (repeatable): overrides the lock inherited from the source job, e.g. --lock gookit/ini so jobs of other sub-modules stop queueing behind the project root. The continuation's cwd is unchanged
job resume	flag max-cost	kill the job once its reported cost exceeds this many USD, e.g. 2.5 (only for agents that report a cost; default unlimited)
job resume	flag max-tokens	kill the job once its token usage (input+output+cache) exceeds this; accepts 50000 / 50k / 1.5m (default: the agent's / project's budget, else unlimited)
job resume	flag max-turns	kill the job once it has made more than this many model requests (default unlimited)
job resume	flag mode	continuation form: session (resident ACP) | interactive (pty) | batch (one-shot --resume -p); default = what the source job implies
job resume	flag model	model for the continuation (default = the source job's model)
job resume	flag no-notify	do not notify the session when the continuation ends (the source job's end-notification is inherited by default)
job resume	flag no-plan	group the continuation under no plan (drops the inherited plan and its checklist link)
job resume	flag plan	plan to group the continuation under (default = the source job's plan)
job resume	flag prompt	prompt text for the resumed turn
job resume	flag runner	target runner (must equal the source job's runner; default = source runner)
job resume	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
job resume	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
job retry	desc	Inspect or cancel the durable retries of a failed job
job retry	help	
job retry	examples	
job retry cancel	desc	Cancel one pending retry so the sweeper will not submit it
job retry cancel	help	
job retry cancel	examples	
job retry cancel	flag config	path to the gofer config file
job retry cancel	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
job retry cancel	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
job retry ls	desc	List a job's retry chain (attempt/state/reason/next run)
job retry ls	help	
job retry ls	examples	
job retry ls	flag config	path to the gofer config file
job retry ls	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
job retry ls	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
job review	desc	Print a job's acceptance材料 in one screen (status / review / verify / commits / usage / diff summary + report tail); --diff adds the full diff
job review	help	
job review	examples	
job review	flag config	path to the gofer config file
job review	flag diff	also print the full diff (the captured changes.diff)
job review	flag json	print the job's id/status and the review hints as JSON instead of the review screen
job review	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
job review	flag tail	how many lines of the agent's final report (stdout tail) to print
job review	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
job run	desc	Submit a new job
job run	help	
job run	examples	
job run	flag acceptance	acceptance criteria (markdown list): appended to the agent's prompt as a 「## 验收标准」 section and shown in review
job run	flag agent	agent key (required)
job run	flag agent-arg	extra arg appended to cli-agent argv (repeatable)
job run	flag agent-budget-cost-usd	soft USD cost budget handed to the agent, which winds the run up itself once spent, e.g. 2.5 (only agents with an agent_budget mapping — others are refused)
job run	flag agent-budget-tokens	soft token budget handed to the agent, which winds the run up itself once spent (accepts 50000 / 50k / 1.5m; only agents with an agent_budget mapping, e.g. suga — others are refused). Keep it below --max-tokens
job run	flag branch	branch name for --worktree (overrides the project's worktree.branch template)
job run	flag channel	submission channel recorded as provenance (cli/web/mcp/...)
job run	flag collect	glob collected from the job's cwd into its artifacts after the job ends (repeatable, e.g. 'tmp/out/*.csv')
job run	flag cols	initial terminal columns for --interactive (0 = server default 80)
job run	flag config	path to the gofer config file
job run	flag cwd	working dir within the project
job run	flag deliver	with --worktree: deliver the branch once done / accepted: none | merge | push | pr (overrides the project's delivery.mode)
job run	flag deliver-branch	with --deliver push|pr: the remote branch name
job run	flag env	extra env var for the job process: K=V (repeatable). The value is stored with the job (request_json) — never pass secrets here
job run	flag exclusive-dir	force the exclusive same-directory lock for this job (an exec job included): no other exclusive job runs in this directory, its ancestors or its subdirectories
job run	flag fallback	comma-separated fallback agents for a transient failure (e.g. omp,claude); overrides the project/agent lists
job run	flag file	submit a md+yaml task file (frontmatter params + prompt body)
job run	flag from-session	start a NEW agent session that inherits this earlier session's context (cli-agent with from_session_args, e.g. suag --from); unlike `job resume` the source session is not continued
job run	flag hold	hold the job for a person's approval: it parks in awaiting_approval and runs only after someone approves it in the web console (or gofer job approve outside an agent session); rejected or expired = cancelled, never run
job run	flag hold-reason	why the job needs approval, shown to the approver (with --hold)
job run	flag hold-timeout	seconds to wait for a decision before the job is cancelled (0 = server.hold.default_timeout_sec, 86400; above server.hold.max_timeout_sec is refused)
job run	flag idle-timeout	seconds to await the next session message (0 = 1800)
job run	flag interactive	request an interactive pty job
job run	flag issue	link this job to a repository tracker issue
job run	flag lock	project-relative directory lock path (repeatable)
job run	flag lock-wait	directory lock wait cap in seconds (0 = no cap, if server allows)
job run	flag max-cost	kill the job once its reported cost exceeds this many USD, e.g. 2.5 (only for agents that report a cost; default unlimited)
job run	flag max-session	whole session ceiling in seconds (0 = unlimited)
job run	flag max-tokens	kill the job once its token usage (input+output+cache) exceeds this; accepts 50000 / 50k / 1.5m (default: the agent's / project's budget, else unlimited)
job run	flag max-turns	kill the job once it has made more than this many model requests (default unlimited)
job run	flag mcp	registry MCP server to give this job (repeatable or comma-separated; adds to the server/agent/project bindings)
job run	flag model	model for the agent (cli-agent: its model_args, built in for claude/codex; acp-agent: picked over the protocol); default = the agent's own
job run	flag no-fallback	do not hand this job to a fallback agent (overrides every configured list)
job run	flag no-mcp	give this job no registry MCP servers (overrides every configured binding)
job run	flag no-notify	do not notify the submitting session when this job ends (a --hold job run from an agent session notifies that session by default)
job run	flag no-retry	never re-run this job after a failure (overrides every configured policy)
job run	flag no-rules	inject no rules for this job (overrides every configured binding; a job credential may not use this)
job run	flag no-scope-discipline	do not append the project's 「交付约定」 (scope discipline) section to this job's prompt
job run	flag no-secret-check	disable the advisory secret-shape scan before submitting this job
job run	flag no-skills	mount no skills for this job (overrides every configured binding)
job run	flag no-stall	never kill this job for silence (overrides --stall-timeout, the agent's and the server's settings)
job run	flag no-verify	do not run the project's default verify step for this job
job run	flag notify	tell the submitting session through the gofer messenger when this job ends (a system notice; off by default because each notice starts a messenger process)
job run	flag notify-session	session id to notify when this job ends (implies --notify); default: the source session, else the agent session this command runs in ($GOFER_SESSION_ID / $CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID)
job run	flag plan	attach the job to a plan (grouping key)
job run	flag prime-keywords	comma-separated subsystems / languages / modules this task touches: the injected tracker-prime matches them (with the title and the prompt head) against the memories' keywords, keys, tags and summaries, injecting the matching ones in full and first (default: $GOFER_PRIME_KEYWORDS)
job run	flag project	project key (required)
job run	flag prompt	prompt text for cli-agent (use -- <argv...> for exec)
job run	flag read-only	run read-only: audit/analysis only, the agent cannot write (cli-agent read_only_args / acp-agent acp.modes.read_only)
job run	flag retry	re-run this job after a failure: <n>[:<b1,b2,...>] (n = total attempts including the first; the backoff table defaults to 30,120,300,900,3600)
job run	flag retry-on	with --retry: only re-run on these exit codes, comma-separated (default: any non-zero exit)
job run	flag review	require human review: on a normal completion the job parks in needs_review until someone accepts or rejects it
job run	flag role	role preset: fills agent/system_prompt/project/tags when unset
job run	flag rows	initial terminal rows for --interactive (0 = server default 24)
job run	flag rule	MANDATORY rule to inject at the top of this job's prompt (repeatable; adds to the server/agent/project bindings)
job run	flag runner	runner key (server = server-local; local is a compatibility alias)
job run	flag scope	declared change scope: path globs relative to the repo root (comma-separated and/or repeatable); changed files outside it are marked in review
job run	flag secret	secret to give this job by name (repeatable or comma-separated; declared under secrets: and allowed by the project; server runner only)
job run	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
job run	flag session	keep an ACP agent in the same job across turns
job run	flag shared-dir	give up the exclusive same-directory lock for this job (share the tree with other jobs, at your own risk)
job run	flag skill	skill to mount into this job's private dir (repeatable; adds to the server/agent/project bindings)
job run	flag source-session-id	authenticated terminal session submitting this job; never the agent target session
job run	flag stall-timeout	kill the job after this many seconds without any output (default: the agent's setting, then the server's)
job run	flag strict-timeout	refuse a --timeout above the applicable limit with an error (naming the limit and its config key) instead of clamping it
job run	flag sync	submit synchronously: server waits for terminal state, then returns
job run	flag system-prompt	resident system prompt injected via the agent (advanced; overrides role's)
job run	flag tags	comma-separated free-form tags for the job (search dimension, e.g. --tags ci,nightly)
job run	flag template	render the prompt from a task-book template (see `gofer template ls`)
job run	flag timeout	job timeout in seconds (0 = server default)
job run	flag title	optional job title
job run	flag todo	run this job for a plan todo: the plan is resolved from the todo, the item turns doing and its outcome/commits are written back to its note
job run	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
job run	flag tracker-id	tracker repository identity used with --issue
job run	flag upload	local file to place on the executing machine: <local path>:<dest relative to the job cwd> (repeatable)
job run	flag var	template variable k=v (repeatable; requires --template/-t)
job run	flag verify	command to run after the agent finishes (shell-words, no shell); a non-zero exit fails the job
job run	flag verify-timeout	timeout for the --verify step in seconds (0 = project default, 600s)
job run	flag wait	poll until the job reaches a terminal state
job run	flag wait-timeout	sync wait cap in seconds (0 = server default 30s)
job run	flag worker-id	target worker id for runner=worker (explicit routing)
job run	flag worker-labels	comma-separated labels to auto-select a worker (runner=worker, when --worker-id is unset)
job run	flag worktree	run in a managed git worktree of the project checkout (branch gofer/<job-id>, kept afterwards)
job run	flag worktree-base	base ref for --worktree (default: the checkout's current HEAD)
job run	flag worktree-name	name of this job's --worktree (fills the project's {name} template; default: the job id)
