job wait	desc	Wait until the given jobs are terminal (all of them, or any with --any)
job wait	help	
job wait	examples	
job wait	flag any	return as soon as ANY of the jobs is terminal
job wait	flag config	path to the gofer config file
job wait	flag interval	poll interval (default 2s)
job wait	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
job wait	flag timeout	give up after this duration (e.g. 90s, 30m); empty or 0 = wait forever
job wait	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
job wakeup	desc	Register an event subscription or timer that resumes a job when it fires
job wakeup	help	
job wakeup	examples	
job wakeup create	desc	Register a wakeup on a job (--kind at|every|cron|event; -m/-f carries the instruction)
job wakeup create	help	
job wakeup create	examples	
job wakeup create	flag after	kind=at: fire after this duration (e.g. 10m, 2h)
job wakeup create	flag at	kind=at: fire at this RFC3339 instant
job wakeup create	flag config	path to the gofer config file
job wakeup create	flag cron	kind=cron: five-field cron expression
job wakeup create	flag event	kind=event: event type(s), comma-separated (e.g. job.terminal)
job wakeup create	flag every	kind=every: repeat interval (>= 60s, e.g. 1h)
job wakeup create	flag file	read the instruction from a file
job wakeup create	flag job-id	kind=event: watch THIS job's events (default: the job the wakeup is on)
job wakeup create	flag kind	at | every | cron | event
job wakeup create	flag message	instruction the continuation receives
job wakeup create	flag mode	once | continuous (default: once, or continuous for every/cron)
job wakeup create	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
job wakeup create	flag status	kind=event + job.terminal: only these terminal statuses, comma-separated
job wakeup create	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
job wakeup create	flag tz	kind=cron: IANA timezone (default: server local time)
