job worktree merge	flag cleanup-others	after merging, force-remove the other fan worktrees (and branches) of the same workflow step
job worktree merge	flag comment	after merging, record this comment on the job
job worktree merge	flag config	path to the gofer config file
job worktree merge	flag note	note for --todo-done (default: `<branch> 合入 <main short sha>`)
job worktree merge	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
job worktree merge	flag squash	squash the selected branch into one commit
job worktree merge	flag todo-done	after merging, mark the job's plan todo done (ignored, with a note, for a job without one)
job worktree merge	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
job worktree rm	desc	Remove a job's managed worktree (refuses uncommitted changes without --force)
job worktree rm	help	
job worktree rm	examples	
job worktree rm	flag config	path to the gofer config file
job worktree rm	flag delete-branch	also delete the branch (the deliverable — only when it is safe to lose)
job worktree rm	flag force	discard uncommitted changes in the worktree
job worktree rm	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
job worktree rm	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
plan	desc	Create and inspect job grouping plans
plan	help	
plan	examples	
plan add-todo	desc	Add a todo to a plan (the item is created pending; --assign describes who runs it once it is ready)
plan add-todo	help	
plan add-todo	examples	
plan add-todo	flag acceptance	acceptance criteria (markdown list); appended to the job's prompt and shown in review. --acceptance "" clears them
plan add-todo	flag acceptance-from-issue	copy the acceptance_criteria of this issue (the current repo's tracker) into --acceptance
plan add-todo	flag after	comma-separated todo ids this item waits for; `prev` = the plan's previous item (the last one by sort)
plan add-todo	flag agent-budget-cost-usd	soft USD cost budget handed to the agent, which winds the run up itself once spent, e.g. 2.5 (only agents with an agent_budget mapping — others are refused)
plan add-todo	flag agent-budget-tokens	soft token budget handed to the agent, which winds the run up itself once spent (accepts 50000 / 50k / 1.5m; only agents with an agent_budget mapping, e.g. suga — others are refused). Keep it below --max-tokens
plan add-todo	flag assign	agent key that runs this item; a ready item with an assignee is dispatched at once
plan add-todo	flag auto	let the chain start this item once its dependencies are done (default)
plan add-todo	flag cmd	argv an exec item runs, e.g. --cmd 'go test ./...' (required when --assign exec)
plan add-todo	flag config	path to the gofer config file
plan add-todo	flag continue	continue the agent session of this todo id instead of starting a new one; `prev` = the plan's previous item (add-todo only); implies --after on it
plan add-todo	flag cwd	working dir within the project (default: the project root)
plan add-todo	flag job	bind the todo to a job id (optional)
plan add-todo	flag max-cost	kill the job once its reported cost exceeds this many USD, e.g. 2.5 (only for agents that report a cost; default unlimited)
plan add-todo	flag max-tokens	kill the job once its token usage (input+output+cache) exceeds this; accepts 50000 / 50k / 1.5m (default: the agent's / project's budget, else unlimited)
plan add-todo	flag max-turns	kill the job once it has made more than this many model requests (default unlimited)
plan add-todo	flag model	model the item's job runs with (cli-agent model_args / acp-agent protocol pick; default = the agent's own)
plan add-todo	flag no-auto	park this item — only a human (or `plan run`) starts it
plan add-todo	flag no-continue	set-todo: stop continuing a predecessor's session (clears continue_from)
plan add-todo	flag note	short remark for the todo (optional); append later with gofer plan set-todo <todo-id> --append-note "..."
plan add-todo	flag prime-keywords	subsystems / languages / modules this item's job is about, comma-separated and/or repeatable: the dispatched job's tracker-prime injects the matching memories in full and first. --prime-keywords "" clears them
plan add-todo	flag project	project this item runs in (default: the plan's project)
plan add-todo	flag review	require human review: on a normal completion the run parks in needs_review until someone accepts or rejects it
plan add-todo	flag runner	runner key for the job (default: the server's built-in local runner)
plan add-todo	flag scope	declared change scope: path globs relative to the repo root, comma-separated and/or repeatable (e.g. 'internal/job/**,web/src/x.vue'); changed files outside it are marked in review. --scope "" clears it
plan add-todo	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
plan add-todo	flag template	task-book template to render this item's prompt from (default: the plan/todo prompt)
plan add-todo	flag timeout	job timeout in seconds (0 = the server default)
plan add-todo	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
plan add-todo	flag var	template variable k=v (repeatable; requires --template)
plan add-todo	flag verify	command run after the agent finishes (shell-words, no shell); a non-zero exit fails the job
