plan set-todo	help	
plan set-todo	examples	
plan set-todo	flag acceptance	acceptance criteria (markdown list); appended to the job's prompt and shown in review. --acceptance "" clears them
plan set-todo	flag after	comma-separated todo ids this item waits for; `prev` = the plan's previous item (the last one by sort)
plan set-todo	flag agent-budget-cost-usd	soft USD cost budget handed to the agent, which winds the run up itself once spent, e.g. 2.5 (only agents with an agent_budget mapping — others are refused)
plan set-todo	flag agent-budget-tokens	soft token budget handed to the agent, which winds the run up itself once spent (accepts 50000 / 50k / 1.5m; only agents with an agent_budget mapping, e.g. suga — others are refused). Keep it below --max-tokens
plan set-todo	flag append-note	append a line to the todo note (mutually exclusive with --note)
plan set-todo	flag assign	agent key that runs this item; a ready item with an assignee is dispatched at once
plan set-todo	flag auto	let the chain start this item once its dependencies are done (default)
plan set-todo	flag cmd	argv an exec item runs, e.g. --cmd 'go test ./...' (required when --assign exec)
plan set-todo	flag config	path to the gofer config file
plan set-todo	flag continue	continue the agent session of this todo id instead of starting a new one; `prev` = the plan's previous item (add-todo only); implies --after on it
plan set-todo	flag cwd	working dir within the project (default: the project root)
plan set-todo	flag max-cost	kill the job once its reported cost exceeds this many USD, e.g. 2.5 (only for agents that report a cost; default unlimited)
plan set-todo	flag max-tokens	kill the job once its token usage (input+output+cache) exceeds this; accepts 50000 / 50k / 1.5m (default: the agent's / project's budget, else unlimited)
plan set-todo	flag max-turns	kill the job once it has made more than this many model requests (default unlimited)
plan set-todo	flag model	model the item's job runs with (cli-agent model_args / acp-agent protocol pick; default = the agent's own)
plan set-todo	flag no-auto	park this item — only a human (or `plan run`) starts it
plan set-todo	flag no-continue	set-todo: stop continuing a predecessor's session (clears continue_from)
plan set-todo	flag note	set the todo note; --note "" clears it (kept unchanged when omitted)
plan set-todo	flag prime-keywords	subsystems / languages / modules this item's job is about, comma-separated and/or repeatable: the dispatched job's tracker-prime injects the matching memories in full and first. --prime-keywords "" clears them
plan set-todo	flag project	project this item runs in (default: the plan's project)
plan set-todo	flag review	require human review: on a normal completion the run parks in needs_review until someone accepts or rejects it
plan set-todo	flag runner	runner key for the job (default: the server's built-in local runner)
plan set-todo	flag scope	declared change scope: path globs relative to the repo root, comma-separated and/or repeatable (e.g. 'internal/job/**,web/src/x.vue'); changed files outside it are marked in review. --scope "" clears it
plan set-todo	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
plan set-todo	flag status	lifecycle status: pending|ready|doing|done|skipped (wins over --undone)
plan set-todo	flag template	task-book template to render this item's prompt from (default: the plan/todo prompt)
plan set-todo	flag timeout	job timeout in seconds (0 = the server default)
plan set-todo	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
plan set-todo	flag undone	mark the todo not done (= --status pending)
plan set-todo	flag var	template variable k=v (repeatable; requires --template)
plan set-todo	flag verify	command run after the agent finishes (shell-words, no shell); a non-zero exit fails the job
