session nudge resume	desc	Resume a paused nudge (failure count cleared, timers restart now)
session nudge resume	help	
session nudge resume	examples	
session nudge resume	flag config	path to the gofer config file
session nudge resume	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
session nudge resume	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
session owner	desc	Hand a session to another caller (admin only; needs can_admin): the way out of a token split, where the hook now reports as a caller the session does not belong to
session owner	help	
session owner	examples	
session owner	flag config	path to the gofer config file
session owner	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
session owner	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
session relay	desc	Set a session's web relay mode auto|on|off (omit --session: the session of the current directory)
session relay	help	
session relay	examples	
session relay	flag config	path to the gofer config file
session relay	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
session relay	flag session	session id (default: resolve by current directory)
session relay	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
session release-takeover	desc	Give a session taken over by a `--resume` pty job back to its original terminal (cancels that job, session returns to idle)
session release-takeover	help	
session release-takeover	examples	
session release-takeover	flag config	path to the gofer config file
session release-takeover	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
session release-takeover	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
session remove	desc	Remove a session registration (its turns stay for audit)
session remove	help	
session remove	examples	
session remove	flag config	path to the gofer config file
session remove	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
session remove	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
session resume	desc	Wake a session up: start a new `--resume` pty process for it (works for ended sessions too); then attach in the web console
session resume	help	
session resume	examples	
session resume	flag config	path to the gofer config file
session resume	flag input	first text typed into the new terminal (optional)
session resume	flag plan	only show whether and how the session could be woken up; start nothing
session resume	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
session resume	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
session say	desc	Answer a session's waiting turn from the CLI (same as the web input box; --deliver also reaches an idle session in tmux)
session say	help	
session say	examples	
session say	flag config	path to the gofer config file
session say	flag deliver	route the reply: answer the OPEN turn if there is one, else type it into the session's tmux pane (§9.1 A)
session say	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
session say	flag takeover	with --deliver: if the session has no usable tmux pane, start a new `--resume` process and send it there (§9.1 B; the original terminal stops relaying)
session say	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
session screen	desc	Print the tail of what a session shows now (recent relay turns, or a takeover pty job's transcript); read-only
session screen	help	
session screen	examples	
session screen	flag config	path to the gofer config file
session screen	flag json	print the screen with its source as JSON
session screen	flag n	how many lines to print (1-500)
session screen	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
session screen	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
session show	desc	Show one session and its recent relay turns
session show	help	
session show	examples	
session show	flag config	path to the gofer config file
session show	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
session show	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
session topic	desc	Record what the current session works on (one sentence) and the sub-paths it owns, so others can find it with `session find`
session topic	help	
session topic	examples	
session topic	flag clear-scope	empty the scope
session topic	flag config	path to the gofer config file
session topic	flag scope	project-root-relative sub-path this session owns (repeatable; replaces the old scope)
session topic	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
session topic	flag session	session id (default: the current session from the environment; never guessed from the directory)
session topic	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
session wait	desc	Block until a session reaches a state (idle | waiting_reply | ended). Exit 0 = reached, 2 = timeout, 1 = error
session wait	help	
session wait	examples	
session wait	flag config	path to the gofer config file
session wait	flag json	print the final session state as JSON
session wait	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
session wait	flag timeout	give up after this long (e.g. 90s, 10m)
session wait	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
session wait	flag until	state to wait for: idle | waiting_reply | ended (comma-separated for several)
session watch	desc	Register a job for the current agent session's Stop-hook completion notice
session watch	help	
session watch	examples	
session watch	flag config	path to the gofer config file
session watch	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
session watch	flag session	session id (default: resolve by current directory)
session watch	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
